dialogue_model.tsv — provenance and licensing
==============================================

What it is
----------
A linear-chain CRF sentence-segmentation model (same format/features as the
crfcut model) retrained for dialogue- and quote-heavy prose (conversational
text, quoted speech). The default crfcut model is trained on TED subtitles and
generalises poorly to this register; this model is the in-domain replacement.

How it was made (recipe)
------------------------
Weak supervision (self-labelled silver corpus), no external gold corpus:

  1. Source text: text we own (used with permission). No third-party corpus is
     used.
  2. Silver labelling (cmd/crftrain): tokenize with the default segmenter
     (whitespace kept) and mark a sentence boundary ('E') using only
     ORTHOGRAPHIC signals that are high-precision in this register:
       - a token ending in a closing quote (” " » 」 』 ’) or terminal
         punctuation (. ! ? … 。 ！ ？), and
       - the token immediately before an opening dialogue quote (“ « 「 『 „).
     Bare inter-word spaces are treated as NON-boundaries (in dialogue-heavy
     Thai prose they are mostly intra-sentence clause separators — the ambiguity
     the CRF resolves). The labelling is independent of the CRF's own lexical
     features, so the before/after comparison is not circular.
  3. Train: averaged structured perceptron (crf.Train), 12 iterations.

Measured quality (held-out silver)
----------------------------------
  - Internal 80/20 split : trained E-F1 0.9652 (P 0.9993 / R 0.9334)
      vs crfcut(TED) 0.1163, whitespace 0.2819.
  - Fully separate file  : trained E-F1 0.9782 (P 1.0000 / R 0.9574)
      vs crfcut(TED) 0.6252, whitespace 0.6586.

Known limitation
----------------
The silver marks dialogue/punctuation boundaries only; pure narration sentences
that end without punctuation or a paragraph break are under-segmented. To improve
recall, re-derive the silver from non-chunked source that preserves paragraph /
line breaks (a strong extra boundary signal) and retrain.

Licensing
---------
Derived from text we own via self weak-supervision. The model stores aggregate
CRF feature weights over short (≤3) word n-grams — statistical parameters, not
reconstructable prose — analogous to the upstream crfcut model. Shippable under
the project licence.

Note on LST20: the LST20 Thai treebank (NECTEC/AIForThai) has explicit sentence
and clause boundaries and is often cited as CC BY 3.0, but its official
distribution terms (aiforthai.in.th) require registration/agreement and state
that "modification and redistribution of the dataset by any means are strictly
prohibited unless authorized by the corpus authors." It is gated (not freely
downloadable) and is NOT used here; a model shipped from it would need NECTEC
authorization. It remains the recommended clean gold corpus IF such authorization
is obtained.
